This comment is a continuation of my review, still pinned to **`7c24b1dfa4f5b5c17b4e942b8dfbddd96a06872c`** as instructed. It adds three things: the end-to-end results I could not previously produce, an upgrade of F-3 from a code-reading observation to an empirically reproduced one, and an explicit note on later working-tree state.

### Method: the frozen checker, run without touching the shared checkout

